# Model checkpoints are large binaries kept out of git.
# Track the directory layout (.gitkeep, README) but not the weights.
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.engine
*.weights

# The shipped FSOCO YOLOv8n checkpoint is tracked (6 MB); other artifacts stay out.
!fsoco_yolov8n/weights/best.pt

# The YOLO26n-pose cone detector (6.2 MB), kept as the keypoint-capable weight.
# It ships in-tree so the node has no dependency on a path outside the
# workspace; a missing weight makes the detector fail at startup and /cones
# publish nothing at all.
!cone_pose_8kpt/weights/best.pt

# The YOLO26n detect-only cone detector the perception node runs by default
# (5.1 MB). Same five classes in the same order as the pose weight, no
# keypoints. Tracked for the same reason as above.
!cone_detect_yolo26n/weights/best.pt

# The final 3-class YOLO26n detect weight (5.4 MB, 2026-08-13 finetune_nano_3cls:
# BLUE/YELLOW/ORANGE) -- the perception node's default model_path. Its
# TensorRT .engine is machine-specific and stays untracked.
!cone_detect_yolo26n_3cls/weights/best.pt
